Engineering is right that a public outage destroys the launch, so we protect the $5k floor. But Sales needs discount funds for paying customers in 90 days. Marketing gets a smaller base now, funded by a reserve unlocked once initial uptime and traffic targets are met. Sales and Engineering will trade: Engineering will embed an engineer into Sales demo calls twice a week to help close complex AI accounts.
  Reserve: $500, released on day 30: Marketing gets the $500 on day 30 if Engineering confirms zero downtime during the first 2 weeks.
  Trade: Engineering provides developer time for Sales custom demo calls twice a week.
  @Engineering: Deliver zero launch-day outages under expected AI interview traffic.
  @Marketing: Optimize the lean initial budget to secure baseline recruiter interest for the webinar.
  @Sales: Convert early pipeline into paying customers within the first 90 days.

Engineering gets $4,750 to secure core QA without risking an outage. Sales holds $3,250 to fund early-customer discounts and drive 90-day revenue. Marketing starts at $1,500 with a $500 reserve tied to launch stability, plus a trade: Sales will share high-intent lead lists to lower Marketing's acquisition costs.
